{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2106","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2106","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2106\",\"parent_revision\":\"25dc5f14dde732b6788d858aedceec7d79f56f49\",\"root_revision\":\"71e2816e8d8ae53869ec239111a4bf8a25a7d05b4708538db912c69854275695\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **surface auto-fix diffs for human approval in /complete-implementation** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 pattern: Auto-Fix with Human Review (Patterns Worth Adopting / Auto-Fix Capability)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-04)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Auto-fix commits that bypass developer review are a trust and correctness risk. When `/complete-implementation` is in a recursion loop, cumulative diffs can be large and include semantically incorrect changes that only a human can assess. The `autonomy: checkpoint` mode exists precisely to give developers control \u2014 but it does not gate auto-fix commits today. Affects every developer running `/complete-implementation` with `autonomy != full_auto`.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Developers using `autonomy: checkpoint` or `autonomy: per_task` who expect review gates before code is committed on their behalf.\\\\n- Bottleneck: The Final Step commit (SKILL.md lines 887-905) is an unconditional sweep \u2014 it runs regardless of autonomy mode and regardless of how many auto-fix iterations T1 completed.\\\\n- Downstream: Any feature going through the T1 fix loop (fires on any `NEEDS-WORK` or `FAIL` verdict from `@dh:code-reviewer`) is affected. T5 doc-regeneration changes also land in the same unconditional commit.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Developers can inspect, edit, or reject auto-fix changes before they are committed, preserving git history integrity.\\\\n- The approval gate is skipped under `full_auto` \u2014 zero regression for fully automated pipelines.\\\\n- Surfacing the diff as a named artifact (`qg-auto-fix-diff`) makes it retrievable by downstream agents and CI for audit.\\\\n- Aligns `/complete-implementation` with the `autonomy` contract that `implement-feature` already honors \u2014 consistent developer experience across both skills.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `Plan.autonomy` is `checkpoint` or `per_task` AND any quality-gate phase produces auto-fix file changes (T1 fix loop, T5 doc-regeneration):\\\\n\\\\n1. All fix-loop iterations complete (up to the 3-cycle max).\\\\n2. Before committing, the skill runs `git diff HEAD` to produce a unified diff of all auto-fix changes.\\\\n3. The diff is registered as an artifact: `artifact_register(type='qg-auto-fix-diff', ...)`.\\\\n4. The skill emits `AUTO-FIX REVIEW REQUIRED` with the artifact path to the console.\\\\n5. The skill halts \u2014 it does NOT commit and does NOT push.\\\\n6. Developer reviews the diff, optionally edits files, then re-runs `/complete-implementation` with an approval signal.\\\\n7. On re-run with approval signal, the gate is bypassed and the Final Step commit proceeds normally.\\\\n\\\\nWhen `Plan.autonomy == full_auto` OR there are no auto-fix changes: the gate is skipped entirely \u2014 behavior identical to today.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable target state after implementation:\\\\n- Running `/complete-implementation` on a plan with `autonomy: checkpoint` and a ruff violation: the skill completes T1 fix loop, then pauses. Console output contains `AUTO-FIX REVIEW REQUIRED`. A diff artifact path is printed.\\\\n- `artifact_list(issue_number=N)` returns an entry with `type: qg-auto-fix-diff`.\\\\n- Re-running `/complete-implementation` with the approval signal proceeds to commit without halting again.\\\\n- New section `Auto-Fix Approval Gate` is present in `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` between the `Completion Verification Gate` and `Final Step` sections.\\\\n- `full_auto` plans and plans with no auto-fix changes are unaffected \u2014 no new pause, no artifact registered.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `/complete-implementation` on a plan with `autonomy: checkpoint` and a deliberate ruff violation: run completes T1 fix loop, then halts. Console output contains `AUTO-FIX REVIEW REQUIRED` and the path to the diff artifact.\\\\n2. `artifact_list(issue_number=N)` for that run returns an entry with `type: qg-auto-fix-diff`.\\\\n3. Re-running `/complete-implementation` with the approval signal bypasses the gate and proceeds to Final Step commit.\\\\n4. `/complete-implementation` on a plan with `autonomy: full_auto` does NOT halt \u2014 auto-fixes are committed without prompting.\\\\n5. `/complete-implementation` on a plan with `autonomy: checkpoint` and a clean T1 verdict (no auto-fixes) does NOT register a `qg-auto-fix-diff` artifact and does NOT halt before Final Step.\\\\n6. Section `Auto-Fix Approval Gate` exists in `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` and documents: diff generation command, artifact registration call, halt condition, and re-run instruction.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Primary skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 612-618 (T1 fix loop), lines 887-905 (Final Step commit) |\\\\n| Model | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` lines 321-327 (`Plan.autonomy` field) |\\\\n| Research | `research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md` \u2014 Auto-Fix Capability with Human Review pattern (lines 94-115) |\\\\n| Related item | #2104 \u2014 Isolated worktree for quality gates (complementary; not a dependency) |\\\\n| Related item | #1859 \u2014 Autonomy modes (prerequisite; status:verified) |\\\\n| MCP tool | `artifact_register(type='qg-auto-fix-diff', content=..., issue_number=N)` \u2014 mechanism for surfacing diff artifact |\\\\n| Artifact type registry | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` section \\\\\\\"Artifact Manifest System\\\\\\\" \u2014 authoritative artifact type list |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: #1859 (Add autonomy modes to implement-feature) \u2014 `Plan.autonomy` field must exist. Confirmed DONE (status:verified; field present at `models.py` lines 321-327).\\\\n- Blocks: None identified in current backlog.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall-Medium \u2014 Three distinct surfaces:\\\\n1. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 new `Auto-Fix Approval Gate` section (prose only, no code): ~0.5 day.\\\\n2. Optional `Plan` model change if approval uses a Plan field: trivial one-field addition, same pattern as `autonomy` at lines 321-327 (~0.25 day including tests).\\\\n3. `artifact_register` call and artifact type registration in CLAUDE.md: minimal effort.\\\\n\\\\nTotal: 0.5-1 day depending on Q1 (approval mechanism) resolution.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Approval mechanism not specified \u2014 see Q1. Blocks writing the `Auto-Fix Approval Gate` section of SKILL.md and any `Plan` model changes required.\\\\n- `qg-auto-fix-diff` artifact type not registered in the authoritative type list in `development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 see Q3. Blocks consistent `artifact_register` calls and the AC2 acceptance test.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- **Q1** \u2014 Approval re-entry mechanism: should the developer signal approval via (a) `--approve-auto-fixes` CLI flag on the skill invocation, (b) a new `Plan` YAML field (`approve_auto_fixes: true`) written before re-run, or (c) an environment variable `DH_APPROVE_AUTO_FIXES=1`? The mechanism determines whether the `Plan` model needs a new field and how the gate bypass is verified in AC3.\\\\n- **Q2** \u2014 Scope of auto-fix capture: does the approval gate cover (a) only T1 fix-loop changes, (b) T1 fix-loop + T5 doc-regeneration changes, or (c) all uncommitted changes at the Final Step? The target state says \\\\\\\"any quality-gate phase\\\\\\\" \u2014 explicit enumeration needed for AC implementation.\\\\n- **Q3** \u2014 `qg-auto-fix-diff` artifact type: should this new type be added to the authoritative artifact type list in `development-harness/CLAUDE.md`? If yes, which item or PR should own that edit?\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Completeness Summary: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\\\n\\\\nGoal: When `Plan.autonomy != full_auto`, pause `/complete-implementation` before committing auto-fix output from the T1 fix loop and T5 doc-regeneration phase. Surface a unified diff to the developer at a known artifact location. Require explicit re-run with an approval signal to proceed.\\\\n\\\\nSuccess output:\\\\n- `/complete-implementation` on a plan with `autonomy: checkpoint` and a deliberate ruff violation: T1 fix loop completes, then halts before commit. Output contains `AUTO-FIX REVIEW REQUIRED` and a path to the diff artifact.\\\\n- Re-run with approval signal lets the run proceed.\\\\n- New `Auto-Fix Approval Gate` section exists in `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`.\\\\n\\\\n**Conditions:**\\\\n\\\\n1. `Plan.autonomy` field | AVAILABLE | `models.py` lines 321-327 confirms `autonomy: Literal[\\\\\\\"full_auto\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"checkpoint\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"per_task\\\\\\\"]` present (added by #1859, status:verified).\\\\n\\\\n2. Auto-fix source points | AVAILABLE | Two places create auto-fix changes without surfacing a diff: (a) T1 fix loop SKILL.md lines 612-618; (b) T5 doc-regeneration; (c) Final Step commit lines 887-905 sweeps all remaining changes unconditionally.\\\\n\\\\n3. Approval flag mechanism | MISSING | No `--approve-auto-fixes` flag or `approve_auto_fixes` Plan field exists. Must be designed.\\\\n\\\\n4. Diff artifact location | MISSING | `qg-auto-fix-diff` not in the authoritative artifact type list in development-harness/CLAUDE.md (current list: feature-context, architect, task-plan, codebase-analysis, T0-baseline, TN-verification, dispatch-plan, audit-report).\\\\n\\\\n5. Git diff generation | AVAILABLE | `git diff HEAD` callable from within the skill at post-fix-loop pause point.\\\\n\\\\n6. Autonomy check insertion point | AVAILABLE | Logical position: between `Completion Verification Gate` and `Final Step: Commit and Push`.\\\\n\\\\n**Decision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS** \u2014 planning can proceed on conditions 1, 2, 5, 6. Conditions 3 and 4 require human input before the gate section in SKILL.md can be written.\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 Auto-Fix Capability with developer approval gate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe fix loop documented at lines 612\u2013618 (Step 1 of Recursive Follow-up Handling) of `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` and the documentation-update phase T5 commit auto-generated changes directly without surfacing the diff for developer approval. The fix loop creates `fix-{slug}-blocking-N` SAM plans, dispatches `dh:task-worker`, and re-runs T1; the developer is not shown the cumulative diff between iterations and has no opt-out short of killing the session. The Final Step: Commit and Push section (lines 887\u2013905) commits remaining changes in a single sweep at the end. The autonomy field (`Plan.autonomy: full_auto | checkpoint | per_task`, mentioned in CLAUDE.md `python3-development` plugin docs) gates dispatch but not auto-fix commits within `/complete-implementation`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `Plan.autonomy != full_auto` AND any quality-gate phase produces auto-fix commits (T1 fix loop, T5 docs regeneration, T2-discovered missing tests), `/complete-implementation` pauses before committing. It writes a unified diff of all auto-fix changes to a known artifact location (e.g., via `artifact_register(type='qg-auto-fix-diff', content=...)`) and emits a console block listing the diff path. The developer either re-runs `/complete-implementation` with an approval flag, edits the diff, or rejects it. A new section \\\"Auto-Fix Approval Gate\\\" between Phase 6 and \\\"Final Step\\\" documents the prompt structure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `/complete-implementation #N` on a plan with `autonomy: checkpoint` and a deliberate ruff violation. The run completes the T1 fix loop, then halts before commit. The output contains \\\"AUTO-FIX REVIEW REQUIRED\\\" and a path to the artifact with the diff. Re-run with `--approve-auto-fixes` (or a new `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_update(approve_auto_fixes=True)` field) lets it proceed. New section \\\"Auto-Fix Approval Gate\\\" exists in `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5cc0a7be6be19082ae5853aa2b1d3f97eb639c9e646c36e579da96749e73a758\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg3d8w\"}"}